00:10:21.036 --> 00:10:24.639
is that I am capable of taking a step back

00:10:24.639 --> 00:10:28.385
and not making the emotional decision.

00:10:28.385 --> 00:10:30.297
This is the real answer, Ruke:

00:10:30.297 --> 00:10:31.573
What I would do is I would say,

00:10:31.573 --> 00:10:32.950
"Okay, what do I wanna do now?

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.206
"Do I wanna go and rebuild VaynerMedia?

00:10:36.206 --> 00:10:37.961
"Do I ..."

00:10:37.961 --> 00:10:40.629
I'd probably call it
"Chuk Media," C-H-U-K,

00:10:40.629 --> 00:10:44.537
just to get the heebie-jeebies
out of the 420 leavings.

00:10:44.537 --> 00:10:46.253
"Or is there something else on my plate

00:10:46.253 --> 00:10:48.484
"that I've learned from now?"

00:10:48.484 --> 00:10:53.037
I would just be reacting to the
best opportunity for my time

00:10:53.037 --> 00:10:55.551
getting close to 40, wanna buy the Jets.

00:10:55.551 --> 00:10:57.871
"What's the best use of my time?"

00:10:57.871 --> 00:11:00.523
If I was to rebuild all over again

00:11:00.523 --> 00:11:02.970
I feel very confident that I could do it.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.200
That's just how I feel.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.537
(strong, beating music)

00:11:05.537 --> 00:11:07.010
- [Voiceover] Sean asks,
"How do you instill

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:10.947
"soul and swagger into a
physical product you create?"

00:11:10.947 --> 00:11:14.608
- Sean, this question is
phenomenal for so many reasons.

00:11:14.608 --> 00:11:17.812
One: The Wednesday before Thanksgiving

00:11:17.812 --> 00:11:20.040
I met with a bunch of new
employees at VaynerMedia,

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.967
and so many of them
talked about this notion

00:11:22.967 --> 00:11:26.024
of loving it here three months in

00:11:26.024 --> 00:11:27.462
because that's usually
when I see somebody,

00:11:27.462 --> 00:11:29.195
two to three months in.

00:11:29.195 --> 00:11:33.763
They're blown away by how
competitive and great everybody is

00:11:33.763 --> 00:11:36.376
but not at the expense of others.

00:11:36.376 --> 00:11:38.169
Whereas every other agency they worked,

00:11:38.169 --> 00:11:40.533
you know, you're killing each
other politically to move up.

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:43.304
You're like climbing the
dead bodies to the top.

00:11:43.304 --> 00:11:46.279
And they're caught off guard by

00:11:46.279 --> 00:11:47.883
what we have here.

00:11:47.883 --> 00:11:51.405
My answer to them is,
"Everything stems from the top."

00:11:51.405 --> 00:11:53.205
And I really believe that.

00:11:53.205 --> 00:11:55.233
I've said four or five times on this show,

00:11:55.233 --> 00:11:59.062
"Everything that is wrong at
VaynerMedia is 100% my fault

00:11:59.062 --> 00:12:00.369
"because I'm the guy."

00:12:00.369 --> 00:12:03.291
And I'm empowering Steve
if things are screwed up

00:12:03.291 --> 00:12:04.936
or anybody else behind me,

00:12:04.936 --> 00:12:09.341
and so I have a very big belief
in what I'm about to say,

00:12:09.341 --> 00:12:14.088
which is products take the
byproduct of its leader.

00:12:14.088 --> 00:12:17.809
So if she has got swag and flavor,

00:12:17.809 --> 00:12:20.637
then her product is gonna
have swag and flavor.

00:12:20.637 --> 00:12:23.681
I truly believe that
physical products, right,

00:12:23.681 --> 00:12:26.735
that physical products
take the personality

00:12:26.735 --> 00:12:28.799
of the people that are dictating it,

00:12:28.799 --> 00:12:32.086
that literally, in essence,
the soul, the swag,

00:12:32.086 --> 00:12:35.290
the vibe, the DNA, is
extracted out of the person

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.238
and put into the product.

00:12:37.238 --> 00:12:38.543
And I've seen it 100 times

00:12:38.543 --> 00:12:40.687
because I think when you pay attention,

00:12:40.687 --> 00:12:43.168
a lot of brands change, and ebb and flow,

00:12:43.168 --> 00:12:46.348
and a lot of times that
coincides with the CEO,

00:12:46.348 --> 00:12:50.112
the CMO, the people really dictating

00:12:50.563 --> 00:12:52.220
the product's course.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.424
You're making decisions.

00:12:53.424 --> 00:12:54.530
Humans are the variable.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.161
This doesn't come alive;

00:12:56.161 --> 00:12:58.091
it's the people behind
it that instill that.

00:12:58.091 --> 00:13:00.091
So the answer to your question is

00:13:00.091 --> 00:13:04.335
the humans behind the
product dictate its outcome,

00:13:04.335 --> 00:13:05.886
period, end of story.

00:13:05.886 --> 00:13:08.532
I truly, truly, truly believe in that.

00:13:08.532 --> 00:13:09.888
Question of the day:

00:13:09.888 --> 00:13:13.314
I'm gonna ask Steve to ask
the question of the day.

00:13:15.612 --> 00:13:17.976
(Steve and Gary laugh)

00:13:17.976 --> 00:13:20.407
- How was your Thanksgiving?

00:13:20.407 --> 00:13:22.419
- That was very sweet.

00:13:22.808 --> 00:13:24.053
(laughter)

00:13:24.053 --> 00:13:25.647
You keep asking questions.

00:13:25.647 --> 00:13:27.486
I'll keep answering them.

00:13:27.486 --> 00:13:29.506
By the way, quick little
question of the day:

00:13:29.506 --> 00:13:32.055
Give me your Jets, Dolphins prediction.

00:13:32.055 --> 00:13:34.445
If you're right you can get drunk.

00:13:34.445 --> 00:13:36.296
